# Submission-time metadata minimization, from chatmail/relay (MIT).
#
# ONLY loaded by the `strict` compose profile. Under `strict`, all mail is
# end-to-end encrypted, the real subject lives in the protected header inside
# the encrypted part, and the outer Subject is already a placeholder -- so
# replacing it costs nothing and denies the server a metadata trove.
#
# It must NOT be used on a permissive/classic server: eeemail sends cleartext
# mail there, and rewriting Subject would destroy real user data.
/^Received:/            IGNORE
/^X-Originating-IP:/    IGNORE
/^X-Mailer:/            IGNORE
/^User-Agent:/          IGNORE
/^Subject:/             REPLACE Subject: [...]
